# Generators: notes the engine writes, the same every run (language.md,
# Notes). prog writes eight bars of chords in the scale, root takes their
# roots for the bass and arp breaks them into sixteenths. A four-note riff
# seeds the lead: markov chains new phrases from it, mutate moves a third of
# its notes, and in the last scene a live walk plays new notes every bar.
# Change a seed (the last number of a call) for another song in the same style.
tempo 122
scale a minor
track kit drums Tr909 Kit909
track pad synth Jupiter8 JupiterPad
track bass synth Sh101 Sh101Bass
track arp synth Juno106 JunoPluck
track lead synth Ms20 Ms20Lead
strip pad: Level 0.6
strip arp: Level 0.6, Send1 0.3
strip lead: Level 0.7, Send2 0.3

clip beat = kit /16
  bd x...x...x...x...
  ch ..x...x...x...x.
  cp euclid(3,8,2)
# Eight bars of chords: the tonic first, the dominant last.
clip chords = pad voicing
  prog(8,5)
# The root of each chord, in octave 2.
clip low = bass
  root(chords,2)
clip ripple = arp
  arp(chords,updown,16)
clip riff = lead
  "a4 c5 e5 [d5 c5]"
clip chain = lead
  markov(1,riff,9)
clip moved = lead
  mutate(riff,35,4)
clip wander = lead live
  walk(a4,8,3)
scene seed 8: beat chords low riff
scene chain 8: beat chords low ripple chain
scene moved 8: beat chords low ripple moved
scene wander 8: beat chords low ripple wander
arrange seed chain moved wander
